+### IP4P endpoints
+
+If your WireGuard server uses NATMap, akira can resolve an [IP4P address](https://github.com/heiher/natmap#ip4p-address) instead of a regular hostname and port. Publish the IP4P value as the domain's AAAA record and omit the port from `Endpoint`:
+
+```ini
+Endpoint = ip4p.example.com
+```
+
+You can also enter the IP4P IPv6 literal directly:
+
+```ini
+Endpoint = 2001::0355:0101:0101
+```
+
+The example above connects to `1.1.1.1:853`. IP4P domains are resolved again on every connection so updated NAT mappings are picked up. On Switch, akira queries AAAA records through the current IPv4 DNS servers, so the Wi-Fi connection does not need an IPv6 address or IPv6 route. Regular `host:port` endpoints are unchanged.
+
 :::warning
-You have to be externally reachable and not behind CGNAT.
+When not using IP4P or another NAT mapping, you have to be externally reachable and not behind CGNAT.
 :::
 
 Your mileage will vary. This is an early release and still jitters, so it's capped to 720p at a max of 15k bitrate. In my tests the actual bitrate negotiated with the PS5 never got past 6k.
